+
+## Legacy iOS rendering report
+
+An iPhone 14 (A15), iOS 16.3.1 report on the legacy renderer shows missing
+character faces/bodies and indoor surfaces viewed from underneath, while UI
+remains readable. Static inspection found missing viewport-swizzle replay,
+shared graphics/compute program state, and ignored indirect-dispatch arguments.
+The focused legacy replay regression covers queue/device origins, facing,
+NEGATIVE_Y, interleaved graphics/compute bindings, GPU-written dispatch counts
+and compute driver-bank dimensions. These are shared NVN semantic repairs;
+their causal relationship to every reported game symptom still needs device
+validation. See the legacy replay entries in
+[rendering](../../../docs/reference/rendering.md#legacy-viewport-swizzle-replay).
+
+The iOS profile selects the existing Playback/MixWithOthers audio-session mode
+so Silent Mode does not suppress game audio. It changes session policy, not PCM
+generation; speaker audibility and the full gameplay route remain device checks.
