+
+### Legacy viewport swizzle replay
+
+- **Symptom:** flipped scene orientation or reversed facing when a draw uses `NEGATIVE_Y`; UI can use a different viewport state.
+- **Cause:** the recorder emits `OP_VP_SWIZZLE`, but legacy replay neither stores nor applies it. Its coverage proof also omitted queue/device raster-origin differences.
+- **Fix:** preserve per-viewport swizzles, apply the existing shared negative-Y viewport mapping and account for its facing reversal in the coverage proof. Unsupported swizzles are reported and cannot prove full coverage.
+- **Validation:** the focused legacy replay regression reads actual pixels for both queue/device origins, both windings, all cull modes and both Y swizzles. Device gameplay remains a separate check.
+- **Found on:** code review of the [Brilliant Diamond iOS report](../../dm/games/0100000011D90000/README.md#legacy-ios-rendering-report); device causality is pending.
+
+### Legacy compute bindings and indirect group counts
+
+- **Symptom:** a compute dispatch is dropped after a graphics program bind, or indirect work executes zero groups.
+- **Cause:** legacy replay shared one effective program between graphics and compute, and ignored `p_dispatch.ind`, whose direct dimensions are zero. The driver-bank dimensions also need the counts at GPU execution time.
+- **Fix:** retain independent compute state, use Metal's indirect dispatch and copy its counts into the compute driver bank in command-buffer order. The CPU fills the rest of that bank without overwriting those twelve GPU-owned bytes. Track storage writes so later CPU proofs cannot read stale vertices.
+- **Validation:** the focused legacy replay regression interleaves and unbinds graphics programs, queues buffer copies with stale CPU destinations, then checks every compute result and the shader-visible driver dimensions.
